  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Farmers and processors pay for dependable water, health and quality management. They judge you by records, results and honesty.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is recording water readings daily and acting on changes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and fisheries science and aquaculture: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools analyse sensor data and summarise records. Routine data summaries shrink.
  </p>
  <p>
    Field judgment, discipline and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to read data and check it; later, own farm decisions.
  </p>

